; AlifeTactics cleanup overlay on ai_tweaks\xr_danger.ltx - paired with the at_danger runtime patch.
; Delete-lines only, no value rows: every detection distance and inertion comes from whichever
; xr_danger.ltx won the MO2 slot (vanilla or any AI overhaul copy) plus later DLTX
; overlays. The setup owns the danger tuning; AlifeTactics owns the reactions and the bug fixes.
; (The 1.1.0 value rows were copied verbatim from a popular AI overhaul and cut vanilla's effective reaction
; ranges 3-50x; removed 2026-07-10.)
;
; The deleted keys are the leftovers of the danger_object enum name collision (danger_object.h:16-27):
; the PerceiveType names hit/sound/visual share values 0/1/2 with entity_attacked/attack_sound/
; bullet_ricochet, so vanilla-derived xr_danger read three danger types from the wrong rows. at_danger's
; bd_types fix redirects those types to their true rows; nothing reads hit/sound/visual after it, and
; these lines drop them from the merged config.
; NOT !![section]: that is DLTX section-DELETE (Xr_ini.cpp:721-739) and would discard the setup's rows.

![danger_inertion]
!hit
!sound
!visual

![danger_object]
!hit
!sound
!visual

